Reuse projected context messages per session entry so idle cache warming survives
boundary context refreshes.

Applies to the published @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent 1.2.0 package (dist/),
both the module build used by Pi Web and the CLI bundle.

The SDK rebuilds custom-message, branch-summary and compaction messages as new
objects on every session projection. Any extension with a turn_end or
agent_before_settle handler (for example pi-goal) triggers such a projection at
each boundary, and the cache warmer's object-identity check then reports
"conversation context changed" and stops idle warming.
Upstream: https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/issues/10956

